<h1>multigraph</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="graph.html"><em>graph</em></a> whose <a href="edge.html"><em>edges</em></a> are unordered pairs of  <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertices</em></a>, and the same pair of vertices can be connected by multiple edges.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> Same as graph, but E is a <a href="bag.html"><em>bag</em></a> of edges, not a <a href="set.html"><em>set</em></a>.  
</p>
<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="graph.html"><em>graph</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="christofides.html"><em>Christofides algorithm</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="hypergraph.html"><em>hypergraph</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
A definition of "pseudograph" is a multigraph that may have <a href="selfloop.html"><em>self-loops</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

